===Etymology 2===
[[Image:Small pitcher Iran Louvre MAO714.jpg|thumb|right|A '''pitcher''' for pouring liquids.]]
[[File:Nepenthes_rafflesiana_ant.jpg|thumb|Ant drinking from the '''pitcher''' (type of plant appendage) of a ''Nepenthes rafflesiana''.]]

From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|picher}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|pichier}}, {{m|fro|pechier||small jug}}, {{m|fro|bichier}} (compare modern French {{m|fr|pichet}}), from {{etyl|LL.|en}} or {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|pīcārium}}, alteration of {{m|la|bīcārium}}, itself possibly from {{m|la|bacarium}}, {{m|la|bacar}} or from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|βῖκος}}. More at {{l|en|beaker}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A wide-mouthed, deep [[vessel]] for holding [[liquid]]s, with a [[spout]] or protruding [[lip]] and a [[handle]]; a [[water jug]] or [[jar]] with a large [[ear]] or handle.
# {{lb|en|botany}} A [[tubular]] or [[cuplike]] [[appendage]] or expansion of the leaves of certain plants. See [[w:pitcher plant|pitcher plant]].

